# Log 319 — test session uses private runtime stores (sec08 order-dependent failure)
date_utc: 2026-10-28T22:34:19Z
base: origin/main e5b1c6674bd977a3eb80b52697db7a3136e3bf8b
python: Python 3.11.17

## Symptom (from log 317 local full run, 3.11)
tests/test_sec08_civilization_admission.py::test_every_civilization_route_is_rate_limited
  [get-/civilization/registry-None] codes [200,200,200]; [post-/civilization/execute-body2] 400 instead of 429.
  Passed alone and in CI. Not reproduced by ordering alone.

## Root cause hypothesis
server._RATE_LIMIT_STORE = RateLimitStore(default_db_path()); default = $TMPDIR/agos_rate_limit.sqlite3
(host-wide, intended for production). The test session used the same host file, so any other
process on the host calling reset() wipes this session's counters. During the log-317 work a
second pytest process existed on the host (a detached run that the sandbox reported as stopped);
that it was alive at the failure moment is INFERRED, not proven.

## Reproduction on main (before fix): concurrent reset loop on the host file
$ python -c "<loop: RateLimitStore(default_db_path()).reset() for 20s>" & pytest tests/test_sec08_civilization_admission.py -k rate_limited
E   assert 400 == 429
    assert codes[2] == 429, codes
E   assert 400 == 429
    assert codes[2] == 429, codes
E   assert 404 == 429
    assert codes[2] == 429, codes
E   assert 404 == 429
======================= 6 failed, 12 deselected in 1.76s =======================

